            <div class="guide-sec">
                <h3>ROLES</h3>
                <b>Game Modes:</b> After START you choose Classic Roles (the original role-based maze run), Blank Slate (only a pistol; every portal opens a shop where you spend points on ONE skill, ONE ultimate and unlimited upgrades -- click an item, then BUY / UPGRADE / SELL for half back) (plus a weapon shop after every boss stage). From stage 6 every second boss is a MIRROR boss that copies your skill and ultimate with telegraphed moves (Kira fights the normal boss) or TD Mode (the four roles become turrets you build on pads, each with its own range; enemies follow a path and explode on the crystal; build and upgrade between waves).<br><br>
                <b>Shotgunner:</b> Armed with Cyber Shotgun and Pistol. <b>E</b> is a Kinetic Dash on a 4s cooldown that refreshes instantly the moment you kill something. Ult: Hyper Plasma RPG.<br>
                <b>Assassin:</b> Armed with Cyber Katana. Press <b>E</b> for Phantom Rush: 3s of hyper speed. Damage still comes from manual swings (left click), but every kill while it's active refreshes it back to a fresh 3s, so a clean chain can keep it running indefinitely. Land at least one kill across the whole activation and it's instantly available again when it ends; zero kills locks it for 7s. Ult (Blade Wave) punches the camera into a brief zoomed, slowed-down cast for under a second before snapping back. Requires Deflection Matrix upgrade to reflect bullets.<br><br>
                <b>Jumper:</b> Armed with the Phase Carbine. Hold <b>E</b> to aim Warp Blink -- a marker slides out along the ground (green = valid, red = blocked by a wall or out of bounds); release to warp there instantly, even through walls, or let go early/on red to cancel for free. Hold <b>F</b> (once Ultimate is charged) to aim Gravity Slam the same way -- release on green to detonate an AoE blast at that spot AND warp there; enemies caught in it who survive are stunned (can't shoot, yellow sparks) for a few seconds. Warp Blink now follows your crosshair: point at the spot on the ground you want, and the range is capped.<br><br>
                <b>Kira:</b> No gun, just a Death Note. Every enemy floats its kill-number above its head (only visible for this role) -- type that exact number on the number keys and it dies instantly, no aiming needed. Backspace clears a digit; typing 3 digits with no exact match resets. Bosses carry a 100-999 number. Ultimate [F], Hyper Cognition: his mind runs so fast the world slows to a crawl around him for 6s -- enemies, their movement and their shots, not you.
            </div>

